\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Ring-based pipeline view linking the 3D inspection object, the 2D working representation, and the label-free decision layer.} (a)~A tunnel-lining ring is a 3D point cloud whose physical components must be recovered as K, adjacent, and base blocks. (b)~The deterministic pipeline unfolds the ring into a panoramic depth map so boundary evidence can be detected in image space. (c)~Detected boundaries define 2D masks; the masks are useful for asset inspection only after they are tied to a stable physical frame through the K anchor. (d)~Intrinsics4Tun adds the deployment-time control layer: candidate0 is produced by stabilisation and absolute-proxy branch selection, while relative-proxy reflection can override candidate0 only when guardrails accept the challenger. The figure is a schematic; quantitative claims are reported in Tables~\ref {tab:stage-decomposition}--\ref {tab:relative-decisions}.}}{5}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ring-pipeline}{{2}{5}{\textbf {Ring-based pipeline view linking the 3D inspection object, the 2D working representation, and the label-free decision layer.} (a)~A tunnel-lining ring is a 3D point cloud whose physical components must be recovered as K, adjacent, and base blocks. (b)~The deterministic pipeline unfolds the ring into a panoramic depth map so boundary evidence can be detected in image space. (c)~Detected boundaries define 2D masks; the masks are useful for asset inspection only after they are tied to a stable physical frame through the K anchor. (d)~Intrinsics4Tun adds the deployment-time control layer: candidate0 is produced by stabilisation and absolute-proxy branch selection, while relative-proxy reflection can override candidate0 only when guardrails accept the challenger. The figure is a schematic; quantitative claims are reported in Tables~\ref {tab:stage-decomposition}--\ref {tab:relative-decisions}}{figure.caption.6}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Intrinsics4Tun as layered ambiguity resolution.} Seeded physical parameters, gravity/K anchoring, and absolute-proxy order switching define candidate0. K-reflection candidates are evaluated only as challengers to candidate0. The relative proxy and guardrails decide whether to accept the challenger or abstain to candidate0. Ground truth is not used inside the decision path.}}{5}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{3}{5}{\textbf {Intrinsics4Tun as layered ambiguity resolution.} Seeded physical parameters, gravity/K anchoring, and absolute-proxy order switching define candidate0. K-reflection candidates are evaluated only as challengers to candidate0. The relative proxy and guardrails decide whether to accept the challenger or abstain to candidate0. Ground truth is not used inside the decision path}{figure.caption.7}{}}
