\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Stage decomposition of the held-out result on 40 K-bearing rings (17 sections). Means and paired bootstrap 95\% confidence intervals are computed on per-ring mIoU. Lift columns are paired differences against the previous layer; CIs and Wilcoxon $p$-values refer to lift $>0$. The combined K-anchored $\to $ candidate0 row collapses the two intermediate layers because the absolute-proxy-only step alone is not separately defended (its standalone CI brackets zero, see footnote). The final guarded-reflection layer is reported descriptively in this table and as an accept/abstain audit in Table~\ref {tab:relative-proxy}; no quantitative held-out lift is claimed for it.}}{8}{table.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:stage-decomposition}{{2}{8}{Stage decomposition of the held-out result on 40 K-bearing rings (17 sections). Means and paired bootstrap 95\% confidence intervals are computed on per-ring mIoU. Lift columns are paired differences against the previous layer; CIs and Wilcoxon $p$-values refer to lift $>0$. The combined K-anchored $\to $ candidate0 row collapses the two intermediate layers because the absolute-proxy-only step alone is not separately defended (its standalone CI brackets zero, see footnote). The final guarded-reflection layer is reported descriptively in this table and as an accept/abstain audit in Table~\ref {tab:relative-proxy}; no quantitative held-out lift is claimed for it}{table.caption.10}{}}
